{"availability":"available","full":"imphillip/clawui","name":"clawui","description":"A better Control UI for OpenClaw — open-source, community-driven UX improvements to the official web dashboard.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-03-01T17:12:29Z","updated":"2026-04-13T11:04:32Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://clawui.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://try.clawui.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:39.577Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:39.577Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:39.577Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:22:39.577Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A standalone web UI for OpenClaw — deployable independently from the gateway.","OpenClaw ships with a Control UI, but it is served directly by the gateway process. This means the UI and the gateway must run on the same machine. clawui breaks that assumption: it is a self-contained static web app that connects to any OpenClaw gateway over WebSocket, from anywhere.","OpenClaw is a self-hosted gateway that connects chat apps — WhatsApp, Telegram, Discord, iMessage, and more — to AI coding agents. It ships with a browser-based Control UI for chat, configuration, sessions, and node management."],"features":["Your gateway runs on a server, headless. You access the UI from your laptop or phone.","You host a single clawui instance on a CDN and point it at whichever gateway you need.","You run multiple gateways (dev, staging, prod) and switch between them from one UI.","Your team shares a gateway but each member uses their own UI deployment."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imphillip/clawui/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b19fb2c65c009f9cafbbdf2391d4e7de3e474afe0d460602eb23267bf2a94db3","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:39.691Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:39.691Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A standalone web UI for OpenClaw —